{"metadata":{"kernelspec":{"display_name":"Python 3","language":"python","name":"python3"},"language_info":{"name":"python","version":"3.13.16","mimetype":"text/x-python","codemirror_mode":{"name":"ipython","version":3},"pygments_lexer":"ipython3","nbconvert_exporter":"python","file_extension":".py"},"kaggle":{"accelerator":"nvidiaTeslaT4","dataSources":[],"isInternetEnabled":true,"language":"python","sourceType":"notebook","isGpuEnabled":false}},"nbformat_minor":5,"nbformat":4,"cells":[{"id":"04293f4b","cell_type":"markdown","source":"# GridMind V5 — Augmentation, Recurrent Refinement, Test-Time Training & Symbolic Search\n\nBuilt from the problems found in V4 (0–1 % exact match, 79 % cell accuracy that a *copy-the-input* baseline nearly matches, validation loss going up while train loss went down).\n\n## What changes vs V4\n\n| # | Change | Why |\n|---|--------|-----|\n| 1 | **Random D4 + colour-permutation augmentation on every episode** (support order shuffled too) | V4 saw ~800 fixed tasks and memorised them. Augmentation gives effectively unlimited, label-preserving data. |\n| 2 | **Uses `train` + `test` pairs of training tasks**, many random (query, support) episodes per task | V4 ignored all `test` pairs and used one query per task per epoch. |\n| 3 | **Recurrent refinement with deep supervision** — the model reads its own previous answer and improves it for `CFG.steps` steps (shared transformer weights) | Replaces V4's one-shot feed-forward guess with an iterative \"draft → look → fix\" loop, the closest thing here to visual reasoning. |\n| 4 | **Copy-prior + changed-cell loss weighting** | Background cells dominated V4's loss/metric. The model now starts from \"copy the input\" and is pushed to get the *changed* cells right. |\n| 5 | **Honest validation**: support = task `train` pairs, query = the real held-out `test` pairs; copy baseline, changed-cell accuracy, exact match with *and* without oracle size; model selection on exact/changed-cell score instead of val loss | V4's metrics hid the failure. |\n| 6 | **Better size inference** (ratio / difference / constant / transposed rules verified on all support pairs) | Colour and size errors are now reported separately. |\n| 7 | **Test-time augmentation** (8 D4 views × colour permutations, probabilities averaged back in the original frame) and **top-2 attempts** | ARC allows two attempts per test input. |\n| 8 | **Test-time training (TTT)**: fine-tune a copy of the model on the task's own demonstration pairs before predicting | The single most effective known trick for ARC-style tasks. Never touches the test input/output. |\n| 9 | **Larger verified symbolic search** (depth-2 programs: D4, scale, tile, mirror, crop, gravity, symmetry fill, enclosed-fill, half-grid boolean ops, + learned colour map) | A program is only used if it reproduces **every** support output exactly. On ARC-AGI-2 *training* tasks this solved ~6 % of test inputs with 100 % precision; on the *evaluation* set it solves ~0 %, as expected — treat it as a precision tool, not a coverage tool. |\n| 10 | **Reasoning visualisation** — plots the grid after each refinement step | So you can actually *see* what the model is doing. |\n\n**Realistic expectations.** ARC-AGI-2 is deliberately hard; a ~3 M-parameter model trained on 800 tasks will score low on the evaluation set. The goal of this notebook is to (a) measure honestly, (b) show a clear improvement over V4 on the validation protocol, and (c) give you the standard ingredients (augmentation, recursion, TTT, program search) to scale from.\n\nSet `QUICK = True` in the first code cell for a few-minute smoke test.","metadata":{}},{"id":"c509f249","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 1. Setup & configuration","metadata":{}},{"id":"30cdb82a","cell_type":"code","source":"# 1. Imports, reproducibility, configuration\nimport os, json, math, random, copy, time, platform, subprocess\nfrom collections import Counter\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom matplotlib.colors import ListedColormap\nfrom scipy import ndimage\n\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn as nn\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\nfrom torch.utils.data import Dataset, DataLoader\nfrom sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split\n\nSEED = 42\nrandom.seed(SEED); np.random.seed(SEED); torch.manual_seed(SEED)\nif torch.cuda.is_available():\n    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n\ndevice = torch.device(\"cuda\" if torch.cuda.is_available() else \"cpu\")\nAMP = device.type == \"cuda\"          # mixed precision only on GPU\nprint(\"Python:\", platform.python_version(), \"| PyTorch:\", torch.__version__, \"| Device:\", device)\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# QUICK=True  -> tiny smoke-test (a few minutes). Set False for the real run.\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\nQUICK = False\n\nclass CFG:\n    # data / grid\n    grid = 30\n    low = 15\n    in_ch = 11\n    n_col = 10\n    # model\n    d = 128\n    heads = 4\n    shared_layers = 2        # transformer layers that are REUSED at every refinement step\n    steps = 4                # refinement steps (recursion depth)\n    steps_max = 12\n    dropout = 0.1\n    max_support = 10\n    # training\n    batch = 4\n    episodes_per_task = 2    # random (query, augmentation) episodes per task per epoch\n    epochs = 50\n    lr = 3e-4\n    wd = 1e-2\n    warmup_frac = 0.05\n    max_support_train = 6\n    changed_weight = 2.0     # extra loss weight on cells that differ from the input\n    patience = 12\n    # inference\n    ttt_steps = 32           # test-time-training steps per task\n    ttt_lr = 1e-4\n    ttt_batch = 4\n    tta_perms = 2            # colour-permutation copies per D4 transform (total = 8 * tta_perms)\n\nif QUICK:\n    CFG.epochs = 2; CFG.episodes_per_task = 1; CFG.ttt_steps = 4; CFG.tta_perms = 1\n    CFG.d = 64; CFG.steps = 2\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:20:41.781512Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:20:41.782149Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:20:55.465352Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:20:41.782103Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:20:55.464574Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Python: 3.13.16 | PyTorch: 2.11.0+cu130 | Device: cuda\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":1},{"id":"6dbbfc88","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 2. Data\nLoads every task as NumPy grids. The train/val **task** split is identical to V4 (seed 42), so numbers are comparable.","metadata":{}},{"id":"83031ad5","cell_type":"code","source":"# 2. ARC-AGI-2 data\nREPO_URL = \"https://github.com/arcprize/ARC-AGI-2.git\"\nPROJECT_DIR = \"/kaggle/working/GridMind\" if os.path.isdir(\"/kaggle/working\") else os.path.abspath(\"./GridMind\")\nDATA_DIR = os.path.join(PROJECT_DIR, \"data\")\n\nif not os.path.isdir(os.path.join(PROJECT_DIR, \".git\")):\n    if os.path.exists(PROJECT_DIR) and os.listdir(PROJECT_DIR):\n        raise RuntimeError(f\"{PROJECT_DIR} exists but is not a git checkout. Use another PROJECT_DIR.\")\n    subprocess.run([\"git\", \"clone\", \"--depth\", \"1\", REPO_URL, PROJECT_DIR], check=True)\n\nTRAIN_DIR = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"training\")\nEVAL_DIR = os.path.join(DATA_DIR, \"evaluation\")\nCKPT_DIR = os.path.join(PROJECT_DIR, \"checkpoints\"); os.makedirs(CKPT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\nOUT_DIR = os.path.join(PROJECT_DIR, \"outputs\");      os.makedirs(OUT_DIR, exist_ok=True)\n\n\ndef load_tasks(folder):\n    \"\"\"-> {task_id: {\"train\": [(in, out)], \"test\": [(in, out_or_None)]}} with numpy int64 grids.\"\"\"\n    tasks = {}\n    for f in sorted(os.listdir(folder)):\n        if not f.endswith(\".json\"):\n            continue\n        with open(os.path.join(folder, f)) as fh:\n            t = json.load(fh)\n        tasks[f[:-5]] = {\n            \"train\": [(np.array(p[\"input\"], dtype=np.int64), np.array(p[\"output\"], dtype=np.int64)) for p in t[\"train\"]],\n            \"test\":  [(np.array(p[\"input\"], dtype=np.int64),\n                       np.array(p[\"output\"], dtype=np.int64) if \"output\" in p else None) for p in t[\"test\"]],\n        }\n    return tasks\n\nTRAIN_TASKS = load_tasks(TRAIN_DIR)\nEVAL_TASKS = load_tasks(EVAL_DIR) if os.path.isdir(EVAL_DIR) else {}\nprint(\"Training tasks:\", len(TRAIN_TASKS), \"| Evaluation tasks:\", len(EVAL_TASKS))\n\n# Same split as V4 (seed 42, 20%) so results stay comparable.\ntask_ids = sorted(TRAIN_TASKS)\ntrain_ids, val_ids = train_test_split(task_ids, test_size=0.20, random_state=SEED)\nif QUICK:\n    train_ids, val_ids = train_ids[:40], val_ids[:20]\nprint(\"Train tasks:\", len(train_ids), \"| Val tasks:\", len(val_ids))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:20:55.466955Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:20:55.467372Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.052334Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:20:55.467341Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.051481Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"Cloning into '/kaggle/working/GridMind'...\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stdout","text":"Training tasks: 1000 | Evaluation tasks: 120\nTrain tasks: 800 | Val tasks: 200\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":2},{"id":"ab6d6ff7","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 3. Encoding and augmentation\nEvery grid → 11×30×30 (10 one-hot colours + valid-cell mask). Augmentations are applied **consistently** to all support inputs/outputs and the query: one of 8 rotations/flips and a random permutation of colours 1–9 (background 0 is kept).","metadata":{}},{"id":"7ef0e4e8","cell_type":"code","source":"# 3. Grid encoding + augmentation (D4 geometry + colour permutation)\nARC_COLORS = [\"#000000\", \"#0074D9\", \"#FF4136\", \"#2ECC40\", \"#FFDC00\",\n              \"#AAAAAA\", \"#F012BE\", \"#FF851B\", \"#7FDBFF\", \"#870C25\"]\ncmap = ListedColormap(ARC_COLORS)\nEYE = np.eye(CFG.n_col, dtype=np.float32)\n\n\ndef encode_grid(grid):\n    \"\"\"int grid [h,w] -> float tensor [11,30,30] (10 one-hot colours + valid mask).\"\"\"\n    h, w = grid.shape\n    out = np.zeros((CFG.in_ch, CFG.grid, CFG.grid), dtype=np.float32)\n    out[:10, :h, :w] = EYE[grid].transpose(2, 0, 1)\n    out[10, :h, :w] = 1.0\n    return torch.from_numpy(out)\n\n\ndef encode_target(grid):\n    h, w = grid.shape\n    t = torch.full((CFG.grid, CFG.grid), -100, dtype=torch.long)\n    t[:h, :w] = torch.from_numpy(grid)\n    return t\n\n\ndef d4_fwd(x, k, flip):\n    y = np.rot90(x, k, axes=(-2, -1))\n    if flip:\n        y = np.flip(y, axis=-1)\n    return np.ascontiguousarray(y)\n\n\ndef d4_inv(y, k, flip):\n    if flip:\n        y = np.flip(y, axis=-1)\n    return np.ascontiguousarray(np.rot90(y, -k, axes=(-2, -1)))\n\n\nIDENTITY_AUG = (0, False, np.arange(10))\n\ndef random_aug(rng):\n    perm = np.array([0] + rng.sample(range(1, 10), 9))   # background colour 0 stays fixed\n    return (rng.randrange(4), rng.random() < 0.5, perm)\n\ndef apply_aug(grid, aug):\n    k, flip, perm = aug\n    return perm[d4_fwd(grid, k, flip)]\n\n\ndef build_episode(support, q_in, q_out, aug):\n    sup = [(apply_aug(a, aug), apply_aug(b, aug)) for a, b in support]\n    qi = apply_aug(q_in, aug)\n    qo = apply_aug(q_out, aug) if q_out is not None else None\n    return sup, qi, qo\n\n\ndef episode_tensors(sup, qi, qo):\n    d = {\n        \"support_inputs\": torch.stack([encode_grid(a) for a, _ in sup]),\n        \"support_outputs\": torch.stack([encode_grid(b) for _, b in sup]),\n        \"query_input\": encode_grid(qi),\n        \"query_size\": torch.tensor(qi.shape, dtype=torch.long),\n    }\n    if qo is not None:\n        d[\"query_target\"] = encode_target(qo)\n        d[\"target_size\"] = torch.tensor(qo.shape, dtype=torch.long)\n    else:\n        d[\"query_target\"] = torch.full((CFG.grid, CFG.grid), -100, dtype=torch.long)\n        d[\"target_size\"] = torch.tensor([1, 1], dtype=torch.long)\n    return d\n\n\ndef collate(batch):\n    B = len(batch)\n    S = max(x[\"support_inputs\"].shape[0] for x in batch)\n    si = torch.zeros(B, S, CFG.in_ch, CFG.grid, CFG.grid)\n    so = torch.zeros_like(si)\n    sm = torch.zeros(B, S, dtype=torch.bool)\n    for i, x in enumerate(batch):\n        n = x[\"support_inputs\"].shape[0]\n        si[i, :n] = x[\"support_inputs\"]; so[i, :n] = x[\"support_outputs\"]; sm[i, :n] = True\n    return {\n        \"support_inputs\": si, \"support_outputs\": so, \"support_mask\": sm,\n        \"query_input\": torch.stack([x[\"query_input\"] for x in batch]),\n        \"query_target\": torch.stack([x[\"query_target\"] for x in batch]),\n        \"query_size\": torch.stack([x[\"query_size\"] for x in batch]),\n        \"target_size\": torch.stack([x[\"target_size\"] for x in batch]),\n    }\n\n\n# quick self-test of the augmentation round-trip\n_rng = random.Random(0)\n_g = np.random.randint(0, 10, (7, 11))\nfor _ in range(20):\n    _aug = random_aug(_rng)\n    _back = d4_inv(apply_aug(_g, _aug), _aug[0], _aug[1])\n    _inv_perm = np.argsort(_aug[2])\n    assert np.array_equal(_inv_perm[_back], _g)\nprint(\"Encoding + augmentation ready (round-trip test passed).\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.053404Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.053724Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.090655Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.053692Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.089741Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Encoding + augmentation ready (round-trip test passed).\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":3},{"id":"3ef08ec1","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 4. Datasets and baselines\nTraining episodes are generated on the fly. Validation uses the real protocol (support = demonstration pairs, query = hidden test input). The **copy-input baseline** shows what a model that learns nothing would score.","metadata":{}},{"id":"e82a56af","cell_type":"code","source":"# 4. Datasets: random augmented episodes for training, honest held-out items for validation\nclass TrainEpisodes(Dataset):\n    \"\"\"Each sample: pick a task, pick ONE of its pairs (train+test) as query, the rest as support,\n    then apply one random augmentation to everything consistently.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, tasks, ids, per_task, seed=SEED):\n        self.tasks, self.ids, self.per_task, self.seed, self.epoch = tasks, list(ids), per_task, seed, 0\n    def set_epoch(self, e): self.epoch = int(e)\n    def __len__(self): return len(self.ids) * self.per_task\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        rng = random.Random(self.seed + self.epoch * 1_000_003 + i)\n        t = self.tasks[self.ids[i % len(self.ids)]]\n        pool = list(t[\"train\"]) + [(a, b) for a, b in t[\"test\"] if b is not None]\n        qi = rng.randrange(len(pool))\n        support = [p for j, p in enumerate(pool) if j != qi]\n        rng.shuffle(support)\n        support = support[:CFG.max_support_train]\n        sup, q_in, q_out = build_episode(support, pool[qi][0], pool[qi][1], random_aug(rng))\n        return episode_tensors(sup, q_in, q_out)\n\n\ndef make_items(tasks, ids):\n    \"\"\"Real ARC protocol: support = the task's train pairs, query = each TEST input.\"\"\"\n    items = []\n    for tid in ids:\n        t = tasks[tid]\n        for q_in, q_out in t[\"test\"]:\n            items.append({\"task_id\": tid, \"support\": t[\"train\"][:CFG.max_support], \"q_in\": q_in, \"q_out\": q_out})\n    return items\n\n\nclass ItemEpisodes(Dataset):\n    def __init__(self, items): self.items = items\n    def __len__(self): return len(self.items)\n    def __getitem__(self, i):\n        it = self.items[i]\n        return episode_tensors(*build_episode(it[\"support\"], it[\"q_in\"], it[\"q_out\"], IDENTITY_AUG))\n\n\ntrain_ds = TrainEpisodes(TRAIN_TASKS, train_ids, CFG.episodes_per_task)\nval_items = make_items(TRAIN_TASKS, val_ids)\nval_loader = DataLoader(ItemEpisodes(val_items), batch_size=8, shuffle=False, collate_fn=collate)\ntrain_loader = DataLoader(train_ds, batch_size=CFG.batch, shuffle=True, collate_fn=collate,\n                          num_workers=0, pin_memory=AMP, drop_last=True)\nprint(\"Train episodes / epoch:\", len(train_ds), \"| Val items (held-out TEST pairs):\", len(val_items))\n\n# ---- Honest baselines on the validation items ---------------------------------------\ndef copy_baseline(items):\n    cells = correct = exact = same_shape = 0\n    for it in items:\n        qo, qi = it[\"q_out\"], it[\"q_in\"]\n        cells += qo.size\n        if qi.shape == qo.shape:\n            same_shape += 1\n            correct += int((qi == qo).sum())\n            exact += int(np.array_equal(qi, qo))\n    return {\"cell_acc\": correct / cells, \"exact\": exact / len(items), \"same_shape_frac\": same_shape / len(items)}\n\nbase = copy_baseline(val_items)\nprint(f\"COPY-INPUT baseline -> cell acc {base['cell_acc']:.1%} | exact {base['exact']:.1%} | \"\n      f\"same-shape tasks {base['same_shape_frac']:.1%}\")\nprint(\"Any model must beat this baseline on *changed cells* and *exact match* to be learning something.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.092856Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.093258Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.109705Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.093232Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.109057Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Train episodes / epoch: 1600 | Val items (held-out TEST pairs): 212\nCOPY-INPUT baseline -> cell acc 71.7% | exact 0.0% | same-shape tasks 68.4%\nAny model must beat this baseline on *changed cells* and *exact match* to be learning something.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":4},{"id":"97895e91","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 5. Model: GridMind V5\nSupport pairs → input tokens + relation tokens (`[in, out, out−in]`) as memory. The query state is refined for several steps; each step feeds the *current predicted grid* back in and the decoder outputs new colour logits (every step is supervised).","metadata":{}},{"id":"0ad390d3","cell_type":"code","source":"# 5. GridMind V5: recurrent refinement model\nclass ConvRes(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, ch, p=0.0):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.f = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(ch, ch, 3, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, ch), nn.GELU(), nn.Dropout2d(p),\n            nn.Conv2d(ch, ch, 3, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, ch))\n        self.act = nn.GELU()\n    def forward(self, x): return self.act(x + self.f(x))\n\n\nclass GridEncoder(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, c):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.high = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(c.in_ch, 64, 3, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, 64), nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Conv2d(64, 64, 3, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, 64), nn.GELU(), ConvRes(64, c.dropout))\n        self.down = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(64, 96, 3, stride=2, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, 96), nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Conv2d(96, c.d, 3, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, c.d), nn.GELU())\n    def forward(self, x):\n        h = self.high(x)\n        return h, self.down(h)\n\n\nclass Pos2D(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, d, g):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.r = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(1, g, 1, d) * 0.02)\n        self.c = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(1, 1, g, d) * 0.02)\n    def forward(self, x): return x + self.r + self.c\n\n\nclass GridMindV5(nn.Module):\n    def __init__(self, c):\n        super().__init__()\n        self.c = c\n        d = c.d\n        self.encoder = GridEncoder(c)\n        self.pos = Pos2D(d, c.low)\n        self.role = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(1, 3, 1, d) * 0.02)          # support-in / relation / query\n        self.pair_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(1, c.max_support, 1, d) * 0.02)\n        self.step_emb = nn.Parameter(torch.randn(c.steps_max, d) * 0.02)\n        self.relation = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(3 * d, 2 * d), nn.GELU(), nn.Dropout(c.dropout),\n                                      nn.Linear(2 * d, d), nn.LayerNorm(d))\n        layer = nn.TransformerDecoderLayer(d, c.heads, 4 * d, c.dropout, batch_first=True,\n                                           norm_first=True, activation=\"gelu\")\n        self.reasoner = nn.TransformerDecoder(layer, c.shared_layers)     # weights shared across steps\n        self.state_norm = nn.LayerNorm(d)\n        # feedback: current predicted grid -> tokens (this is how the model \"looks at its own answer\")\n        self.feedback = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(c.in_ch, 32, 3, padding=1), nn.GELU(),\n            nn.Conv2d(32, d, 3, stride=2, padding=1), nn.GroupNorm(8, d), nn.GELU())\n        self.decoder = nn.Sequential(\n            nn.Conv2d(d + 64 + c.in_ch + c.n_col, 128, 3, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, 128), nn.GELU(),\n            ConvRes(128, c.dropout),\n            nn.Conv2d(128, 96, 3, padding=1, bias=False), nn.GroupNorm(8, 96), nn.GELU(),\n            ConvRes(96, c.dropout),\n            nn.Conv2d(96, c.n_col, 1))\n        self.copy_gain = nn.Parameter(torch.tensor(2.0))                  # start from \"copy the input\"\n        self.size_head = nn.Sequential(nn.Linear(2 * d, d), nn.GELU(), nn.Dropout(c.dropout),\n                                       nn.Linear(d, 2 * c.grid))\n\n    def tokens(self, x):\n        high, low = self.encoder(x)\n        b, d, h, w = low.shape\n        t = self.pos(low.permute(0, 2, 3, 1))\n        return high, t.reshape(b, h * w, d)\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def tok_mask(x):\n        return F.max_pool2d(x[:, 10:11], 2, 2).flatten(1) > 0\n\n    def encode_support(self, sx, sy, smask):\n        b, s, ch, h, w = sx.shape\n        d = self.c.d\n        _, tx = self.tokens(sx.reshape(b * s, ch, h, w))\n        _, ty = self.tokens(sy.reshape(b * s, ch, h, w))\n        tx, ty = tx.reshape(b, s, -1, d), ty.reshape(b, s, -1, d)\n        pair = self.pair_emb[:, :s]\n        inp = tx + self.role[:, 0] + pair\n        rel = self.relation(torch.cat([tx, ty, ty - tx], dim=-1)) + self.role[:, 1] + pair\n        memory = torch.cat([inp, rel], dim=2).reshape(b, s * 2 * 225, d)\n        im = self.tok_mask(sx.reshape(b * s, ch, h, w)).reshape(b, s, 225)\n        om = self.tok_mask(sy.reshape(b * s, ch, h, w)).reshape(b, s, 225)\n        mm = torch.cat([im, im | om], dim=2) & smask.unsqueeze(-1)\n        return memory, ~mm.reshape(b, s * 450)          # (memory, key_padding_mask)\n\n    def forward(self, sx, sy, qx, smask, steps=None):\n        steps = steps or self.c.steps\n        b = qx.shape[0]\n        d, low = self.c.d, self.c.low\n        memory, mem_pad = self.encode_support(sx, sy, smask)\n        q_high, qt = self.tokens(qx)\n        qt = qt + self.role[:, 2]\n        qmask = self.tok_mask(qx)\n        state, probs, outs = qt, qx[:, :10], []\n        for t in range(steps):\n            fb = self.feedback(torch.cat([probs, qx[:, 10:11]], dim=1))\n            state = state + fb.permute(0, 2, 3, 1).reshape(b, low * low, d) + self.step_emb[t]\n            state = self.reasoner(state, memory, tgt_key_padding_mask=~qmask, memory_key_padding_mask=mem_pad)\n            r = self.state_norm(state)\n            spatial = F.interpolate(r.transpose(1, 2).reshape(b, d, low, low),\n                                    size=(self.c.grid, self.c.grid), mode=\"bilinear\", align_corners=False)\n            logits = self.decoder(torch.cat([spatial, q_high, qx, probs], dim=1)) + self.copy_gain * qx[:, :10]\n            outs.append(logits)\n            probs = F.softmax(logits.float(), dim=1).detach()\n        v = qmask.unsqueeze(-1).to(r.dtype)\n        den = v.sum(1).clamp(min=1.0)\n        pooled = torch.cat([(qt * v).sum(1) / den, (r * v).sum(1) / den], dim=-1)\n        sz = self.size_head(pooled)\n        return {\"logits\": outs, \"height_logits\": sz[:, :self.c.grid], \"width_logits\": sz[:, self.c.grid:]}\n\n\nmodel = GridMindV5(CFG).to(device)\nprint(\"GridMind V5 parameters:\", f\"{sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters()):,}\")\n\n# shape smoke test\n_b = collate([ItemEpisodes(val_items)[0], ItemEpisodes(val_items)[1]])\nwith torch.no_grad():\n    _o = model.eval()(_b[\"support_inputs\"].to(device), _b[\"support_outputs\"].to(device),\n                      _b[\"query_input\"].to(device), _b[\"support_mask\"].to(device))\nassert len(_o[\"logits\"]) == CFG.steps and _o[\"logits\"][0].shape == (2, 10, 30, 30)\nprint(\"Forward pass OK:\", len(_o[\"logits\"]), \"refinement steps ->\", tuple(_o[\"logits\"][-1].shape))\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.110937Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.111767Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.282927Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:20:57.111732Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.282066Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"GridMind V5 parameters: 1,852,103\nForward pass OK: 4 refinement steps -> (2, 10, 30, 30)\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":5},{"id":"f333cac4","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 6. Size inference and loss\nLoss = step-weighted cross-entropy (extra weight on cells that differ from the input) + size heads.","metadata":{}},{"id":"4252e4e1","cell_type":"code","source":"# 6. Output-size inference (rules from the support pairs, neural fallback) + loss\ndef infer_size(support, q_in_shape, neural_hw):\n    \"\"\"Per-axis rules checked on ALL support pairs: constant ratio, constant difference,\n    constant output size, or transposed ratio. Falls back to the neural size head.\"\"\"\n    ins = [a.shape for a, _ in support]\n    outs = [b.shape for _, b in support]\n    res = []\n    for ax in (0, 1):\n        iv, ov = [s[ax] for s in ins], [s[ax] for s in outs]\n        oiv = [s[1 - ax] for s in ins]\n        q, oq = q_in_shape[ax], q_in_shape[1 - ax]\n        pred = None\n        ratios = [o / i for o, i in zip(ov, iv)]\n        if max(ratios) - min(ratios) < 1e-9:\n            v = q * ratios[0]\n            if abs(v - round(v)) < 1e-6:\n                pred = int(round(v))\n        if pred is None:\n            diffs = {o - i for o, i in zip(ov, iv)}\n            if len(diffs) == 1:\n                pred = q + diffs.pop()\n        if pred is None and len(set(ov)) == 1:\n            pred = ov[0]\n        if pred is None:\n            rs = [o / i for o, i in zip(ov, oiv)]\n            if max(rs) - min(rs) < 1e-9:\n                v = oq * rs[0]\n                if abs(v - round(v)) < 1e-6:\n                    pred = int(round(v))\n        res.append(pred if pred is not None and 1 <= pred <= CFG.grid else None)\n    h, w = res\n    if h is not None and w is not None:\n        return h, w, \"rule\"\n    return (h if h is not None else neural_hw[0]), (w if w is not None else neural_hw[1]), \\\n           (\"partial\" if (h is not None or w is not None) else \"neural\")\n\n\ndef compute_loss(out, batch):\n    tgt = batch[\"query_target\"].to(device)\n    ts = batch[\"target_size\"].to(device)\n    qx = batch[\"query_input\"].to(device)\n    in_col = torch.where(qx[:, 10] > 0.5, qx[:, :10].argmax(1), torch.full_like(tgt, -1))\n    valid = tgt != -100\n    changed = valid & (tgt != in_col)\n    w = (1.0 + CFG.changed_weight * changed.float()) * valid.float()\n    denom = w.sum().clamp(min=1.0)\n    T = len(out[\"logits\"])\n    step_w = torch.arange(1, T + 1, device=device, dtype=torch.float32)\n    step_w = step_w / step_w.sum()                       # later refinement steps matter more\n    colour = 0.0\n    for t, lg in enumerate(out[\"logits\"]):\n        ce = F.cross_entropy(lg.float(), tgt, ignore_index=-100, reduction=\"none\")\n        colour = colour + step_w[t] * (ce * w).sum() / denom\n    hl = F.cross_entropy(out[\"height_logits\"].float(), ts[:, 0] - 1)\n    wl = F.cross_entropy(out[\"width_logits\"].float(), ts[:, 1] - 1)\n    return colour + 0.5 * (hl + wl), colour.detach(), (hl + wl).detach()\n\nprint(\"Size inference + loss ready.\")\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.284078Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.284572Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.299322Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.284546Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.298656Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","text":"Size inference + loss ready.\n","output_type":"stream"}],"execution_count":6},{"id":"4a494e78","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 7. Verified symbolic program search\nUsed first at inference. If a program explains all demonstration pairs and gives an unambiguous answer, it is used directly; otherwise the neural model takes over.","metadata":{}},{"id":"30293b21","cell_type":"code","source":"# ---------- Symbolic program search (verified on EVERY support pair) ----------\n# A \"program\" = up to SYM_MAX_DEPTH primitives followed by a learned colour map.\n# A program is only used if it reproduces ALL support outputs exactly.\nSYM_MAX_DEPTH = 2\nSYM_TIME_LIMIT = 3.0   # seconds per query\n\ndef _crop_bbox(g):\n    ys, xs = np.where(g != 0)\n    if len(ys) == 0:\n        return None\n    return g[ys.min():ys.max() + 1, xs.min():xs.max() + 1]\n\ndef _crop_object(g, which):\n    mask = g != 0\n    if not mask.any():\n        return None\n    lab, n = ndimage.label(mask, structure=np.ones((3, 3)))\n    if n == 0:\n        return None\n    sizes = ndimage.sum(mask, lab, range(1, n + 1))\n    target = sizes.max() if which == \"largest\" else sizes.min()\n    ids = [i + 1 for i, s in enumerate(sizes) if s == target]\n    if len(ids) != 1:            # ambiguous -> refuse\n        return None\n    ys, xs = np.where(lab == ids[0])\n    return g[ys.min():ys.max() + 1, xs.min():xs.max() + 1]\n\ndef _gravity(g, d):\n    r = np.rot90(g, d)\n    out = np.zeros_like(r)\n    for j in range(r.shape[1]):\n        col = r[:, j]\n        nz = col[col != 0]\n        if len(nz):\n            out[-len(nz):, j] = nz\n    return np.ascontiguousarray(np.rot90(out, -d))\n\ndef _sym_fill(g, mode):\n    flips = {\n        \"lr\":   [np.fliplr(g)],\n        \"ud\":   [np.flipud(g)],\n        \"both\": [np.fliplr(g), np.flipud(g), np.rot90(g, 2)],\n    }[mode]\n    out = g.copy()\n    for f in flips:\n        m = out == 0\n        out[m] = f[m]\n    return out\n\ndef _fill_enclosed(g):\n    lab, n = ndimage.label(g == 0)\n    border = set(lab[0, :]) | set(lab[-1, :]) | set(lab[:, 0]) | set(lab[:, -1])\n    out = g.copy()\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        if i not in border:\n            out[lab == i] = 10        # special marker; colour-map decides final colour\n    return out\n\ndef _half_op(g, axis, op):\n    n = g.shape[axis]\n    if n < 2:\n        return None\n    if n % 2 == 0:\n        a, b = np.split(g, 2, axis=axis)\n    else:\n        m = n // 2\n        a = g[:m] if axis == 0 else g[:, :m]\n        b = g[m + 1:] if axis == 0 else g[:, m + 1:]\n    ma, mb = a != 0, b != 0\n    res = {\n        \"and\": ma & mb, \"or\": ma | mb, \"xor\": ma ^ mb, \"nor\": ~(ma | mb),\n        \"a_only\": ma & ~mb, \"b_only\": mb & ~ma,\n    }[op]\n    return res.astype(np.int64)\n\ndef _build_primitives():\n    P = {}\n    for k in range(4):\n        for fl in (False, True):\n            if k == 0 and not fl:\n                continue\n            P[f\"d4_{k}_{int(fl)}\"] = (lambda g, k=k, fl=fl: np.ascontiguousarray(\n                np.fliplr(np.rot90(g, k)) if fl else np.rot90(g, k)))\n    for k in (2, 3, 4, 5):\n        P[f\"up{k}\"] = lambda g, k=k: np.kron(g, np.ones((k, k), dtype=np.int64)) if g.shape[0] * k <= 30 and g.shape[1] * k <= 30 else None\n    for k in (2, 3):\n        P[f\"down{k}\"] = lambda g, k=k: g[::k, ::k] if g.shape[0] % k == 0 and g.shape[1] % k == 0 else None\n    for (a, b) in [(1, 2), (2, 1), (2, 2), (3, 3), (1, 3), (3, 1)]:\n        P[f\"tile{a}x{b}\"] = lambda g, a=a, b=b: np.tile(g, (a, b)) if g.shape[0] * a <= 30 and g.shape[1] * b <= 30 else None\n    def _mirror(g, mode):\n        if mode == \"h\":   out = np.hstack([g, np.fliplr(g)])\n        elif mode == \"h2\": out = np.hstack([np.fliplr(g), g])\n        elif mode == \"v\":  out = np.vstack([g, np.flipud(g)])\n        elif mode == \"v2\": out = np.vstack([np.flipud(g), g])\n        else:\n            top = np.hstack([g, np.fliplr(g)])\n            out = np.vstack([top, np.flipud(top)])\n        return out if out.shape[0] <= 30 and out.shape[1] <= 30 else None\n    for m in (\"h\", \"h2\", \"v\", \"v2\", \"quad\"):\n        P[f\"mirror_{m}\"] = lambda g, m=m: _mirror(g, m)\n    P[\"crop_bbox\"] = _crop_bbox\n    P[\"crop_largest\"] = lambda g: _crop_object(g, \"largest\")\n    P[\"crop_smallest\"] = lambda g: _crop_object(g, \"smallest\")\n    for d in range(4):\n        P[f\"gravity{d}\"] = lambda g, d=d: _gravity(g, d)\n    for m in (\"lr\", \"ud\", \"both\"):\n        P[f\"symfill_{m}\"] = lambda g, m=m: _sym_fill(g, m)\n    P[\"fill_enclosed\"] = _fill_enclosed\n    for ax in (0, 1):\n        for op in (\"and\", \"or\", \"xor\", \"nor\", \"a_only\", \"b_only\"):\n            P[f\"half{ax}_{op}\"] = lambda g, ax=ax, op=op: _half_op(g, ax, op)\n    return P\n\nPRIMS = _build_primitives()\n\n\ndef _safe(fn, g):\n    try:\n        out = fn(g)\n    except Exception:\n        return None\n    if out is None or out.ndim != 2 or out.size == 0:\n        return None\n    if out.shape[0] > 30 or out.shape[1] > 30:\n        return None\n    return np.asarray(out, dtype=np.int64)\n\n\ndef _fit_colour_map(srcs, dsts):\n    s = np.concatenate([x.ravel() for x in srcs])\n    d = np.concatenate([x.ravel() for x in dsts])\n    pairs = np.unique(np.stack([s, d], axis=1), axis=0)\n    if len(set(pairs[:, 0].tolist())) != len(pairs):\n        return None\n    return {int(a): int(b) for a, b in pairs}\n\n\ndef _apply_colour_map(g, cmap):\n    identity = all(a == b for a, b in cmap.items() if a <= 9)\n    lut = np.arange(11)\n    for c in np.unique(g):\n        c = int(c)\n        if c in cmap:\n            lut[c] = cmap[c]\n        elif identity and c <= 9:\n            lut[c] = c\n        else:\n            return None\n    return lut[g]\n\n\ndef _try_program(chain_outs_support, chain_out_query, dsts):\n    \"\"\"chain_outs_support: transformed support inputs; returns candidate query output or None.\"\"\"\n    for o, d in zip(chain_outs_support, dsts):\n        if o.shape != d.shape:\n            return None\n    cmap = _fit_colour_map(chain_outs_support, dsts)\n    if cmap is None:\n        return None\n    # verify on every support pair\n    for o, d in zip(chain_outs_support, dsts):\n        pred = _apply_colour_map(o, cmap)\n        if pred is None or not np.array_equal(pred, d):\n            return None\n    return _apply_colour_map(chain_out_query, cmap)\n\n\ndef symbolic_solve(support, q_in, max_depth=None, time_limit=None):\n    \"\"\"Returns (list_of_candidate_grids_ranked, program_name_or_status).\"\"\"\n    max_depth = SYM_MAX_DEPTH if max_depth is None else max_depth\n    time_limit = SYM_TIME_LIMIT if time_limit is None else time_limit\n    t0 = time.time()\n    srcs = [a for a, _ in support]\n    dsts = [b for _, b in support]\n    if not srcs:\n        return [], \"no_support\"\n\n    level = {\"identity\": (srcs, q_in)}\n    for depth in range(0, max_depth + 1):\n        found = []   # (program_name, candidate)\n        for name, (outs, qout) in level.items():\n            cand = _try_program(outs, qout, dsts)\n            if cand is not None:\n                found.append((name, cand))\n        if found:\n            votes = Counter()\n            first = {}\n            for name, cand in found:\n                key = (cand.shape, cand.tobytes())\n                votes[key] += 1\n                first.setdefault(key, (name, cand))\n            ranked = [first[k][1] for k, _ in votes.most_common()]\n            status = first[votes.most_common(1)[0][0]][0]\n            if len(ranked) > 1:\n                status += \"|ambiguous\"\n            return ranked, status\n        if depth == max_depth:\n            break\n        # expand one more primitive\n        nxt = {}\n        for name, (outs, qout) in level.items():\n            for pname, fn in PRIMS.items():\n                if time.time() - t0 > time_limit:\n                    return [], \"timeout\"\n                new_outs = []\n                ok = True\n                for o in outs:\n                    r = _safe(fn, o)\n                    if r is None:\n                        ok = False\n                        break\n                    new_outs.append(r)\n                    if len(new_outs) == 1 and r.shape != dsts[0].shape and depth + 1 == max_depth:\n                        ok = False   # last level: shape must already match the target\n                        break\n                if not ok:\n                    continue\n                qn = _safe(fn, qout)\n                if qn is None:\n                    continue\n                nname = pname if name == \"identity\" else f\"{name}>{pname}\"\n                nxt[nname] = (new_outs, qn)\n        level = nxt\n    return [], \"no_program\"\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.300522Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.300846Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.339519Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.300816Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.338746Z"}},"outputs":[],"execution_count":7},{"id":"2a2b2b52","cell_type":"markdown","source":"## 8. Training\nOne-cycle LR schedule, mixed precision on GPU, augmentation on every episode. The best checkpoint is chosen by **exact match (oracle size) + changed-cell accuracy** on validation, not by loss.","metadata":{}},{"id":"ede09298","cell_type":"code","source":"# 8. Training (AMP, OneCycle schedule, deep supervision, augmentation every episode)\ndef predict_grids(out, batch, support_lists=None):\n    \"\"\"Last-step argmax grids cropped to inferred sizes. Returns list of (pred_grid, size_source).\"\"\"\n    pred = out[\"logits\"][-1].argmax(1).cpu().numpy()\n    nh = out[\"height_logits\"].argmax(1).cpu().numpy() + 1\n    nw = out[\"width_logits\"].argmax(1).cpu().numpy() + 1\n    return pred, nh, nw\n\n\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef evaluate_fast(model, loader, items):\n    \"\"\"Single forward pass, no TTA/TTT. Reports honest metrics.\"\"\"\n    model.eval()\n    n = cells = cell_ok = chg = chg_ok = exact = exact_oracle = size_ok_rule = size_ok_neural = 0\n    k = 0\n    for batch in loader:\n        with torch.autocast(device_type=device.type, dtype=torch.float16, enabled=AMP):\n            out = model(batch[\"support_inputs\"].to(device), batch[\"support_outputs\"].to(device),\n                        batch[\"query_input\"].to(device), batch[\"support_mask\"].to(device))\n        pred, nh, nw = predict_grids(out, batch)\n        for i in range(pred.shape[0]):\n            it = items[k]; k += 1\n            qo, qi = it[\"q_out\"], it[\"q_in\"]\n            th, tw = qo.shape\n            ph, pw, _ = infer_size(it[\"support\"], qi.shape, (int(nh[i]), int(nw[i])))\n            size_ok_rule += (ph, pw) == (th, tw)\n            size_ok_neural += (int(nh[i]), int(nw[i])) == (th, tw)\n            p_or = pred[i, :th, :tw]                        # oracle-size crop: separates colour from size errors\n            cells += qo.size; cell_ok += int((p_or == qo).sum())\n            if qi.shape == qo.shape:\n                m = qi != qo\n                chg += int(m.sum()); chg_ok += int(((p_or == qo) & m).sum())\n            exact_oracle += int(np.array_equal(p_or, qo))\n            exact += int((ph, pw) == (th, tw) and np.array_equal(pred[i, :ph, :pw], qo))\n            n += 1\n    return {\"cell_acc\": cell_ok / cells, \"changed_cell_acc\": chg_ok / max(chg, 1),\n            \"exact\": exact / n, \"exact_oracle_size\": exact_oracle / n,\n            \"size_rule_acc\": size_ok_rule / n, \"size_neural_acc\": size_ok_neural / n}\n\n\ndef make_scaler():\n    try:\n        return torch.amp.GradScaler(\"cuda\", enabled=AMP)\n    except Exception:\n        return torch.cuda.amp.GradScaler(enabled=AMP)\n\n\nBEST_PATH = os.path.join(CKPT_DIR, \"gridmind_v5_best.pt\")\nsteps_total = CFG.epochs * len(train_loader)\noptimizer = torch.optim.AdamW(model.parameters(), lr=CFG.lr, weight_decay=CFG.wd)\nscheduler = torch.optim.lr_scheduler.OneCycleLR(\n    optimizer, max_lr=CFG.lr, total_steps=steps_total, pct_start=max(CFG.warmup_frac, 3.0 / steps_total), anneal_strategy=\"cos\")\nscaler = make_scaler()\n\nhistory, best_score, bad = [], -1.0, 0\nt_start = time.time()\nfor epoch in range(CFG.epochs):\n    train_ds.set_epoch(epoch)\n    model.train()\n    run = nb = 0\n    for batch in train_loader:\n        optimizer.zero_grad(set_to_none=True)\n        with torch.autocast(device_type=device.type, dtype=torch.float16, enabled=AMP):\n            out = model(batch[\"support_inputs\"].to(device), batch[\"support_outputs\"].to(device),\n                        batch[\"query_input\"].to(device), batch[\"support_mask\"].to(device))\n        loss, _, _ = compute_loss(out, batch)\n        scaler.scale(loss).backward()\n        scaler.unscale_(optimizer)\n        nn.utils.clip_grad_norm_(model.parameters(), 1.0)\n        scaler.step(optimizer); scaler.update(); scheduler.step()\n        run += loss.item(); nb += 1\n    m = evaluate_fast(model, val_loader, val_items)\n    score = m[\"exact_oracle_size\"] + m[\"changed_cell_acc\"]          # model selection on real signal, not val loss\n    history.append({\"epoch\": epoch + 1, \"train_loss\": run / max(nb, 1), **m})\n    print(f\"Ep {epoch+1:02d}/{CFG.epochs} | loss {run/max(nb,1):.3f} | cell {m['cell_acc']:.1%} | \"\n          f\"changed-cell {m['changed_cell_acc']:.1%} | exact(oracle size) {m['exact_oracle_size']:.1%} | \"\n          f\"exact {m['exact']:.1%} | size rule/neural {m['size_rule_acc']:.0%}/{m['size_neural_acc']:.0%} | \"\n          f\"{(time.time()-t_start)/60:.1f} min\")\n    if score > best_score:\n        best_score, bad = score, 0\n        torch.save({\"model\": model.state_dict(), \"epoch\": epoch + 1, \"metrics\": m}, BEST_PATH)\n        print(\"   best checkpoint saved\")\n    else:\n        bad += 1\n        if bad >= CFG.patience:\n            print(\"Early stopping.\"); break\nprint(\"Training done. Best selection score:\", round(best_score, 4))\n\nck = torch.load(BEST_PATH, map_location=device)\nmodel.load_state_dict(ck[\"model\"])\nBASE_STATE = copy.deepcopy(model.state_dict())      # untouched copy used by test-time training\nprint(\"Loaded best checkpoint from epoch\", ck[\"epoch\"])\n","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.340609Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.340968Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-07T06:38:36.471869Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-07T06:21:07.340934Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-07T06:38:36.470699Z"}},"outputs":[{"name":"stderr","text":"/tmp/ipykernel_49/4266294644.py:70: UserWarning: Detected call of `lr_scheduler.step()` before `optimizer.step()`. In PyTorch 1.1.0 and later, you should call them in the opposite order: `optimizer.step()` before `lr_scheduler.step()`.  Failure to do this will result in PyTorch skipping the first value of the learning rate schedule. See more details at https://pytorch.org/docs/stable/optim.html#how-to-adjust-learning-rate\n  scaler.step(optimizer); scaler.update(); scheduler.step()\n","output_type":"stream"},{"name":"stdout","text":"Ep 01/50 | loss 4.804 | cell 77.8% | changed-cell 0.0% | exact(oracle size) 0.0% | exact 0.0% | size rule/neural 84%/13% | 0.6 min\n   best checkpoint saved\nEp 02/50 | loss 3.981 | cell 77.1% | changed-cell 0.0% | exact(oracle size) 0.0% | exact 0.0% | size rule/neural 84%/25% | 1.1 min\n   best checkpoint saved\nEp 03/50 | loss 3.464 | cell 77.7% | changed-cell 0.0% | exact(oracle size) 0.0% | exact 0.0% | size